INFO:supervisor:Supervisor created execution plan (goal='Locate single-month volume anomalies in offline_data/regional_sales.csv by computing each region×product_line monthly volume as a multiple of its own 24-month mean, report the top-3 combinations with their multiples and corresponding-month return rates, and judge whether each spike is more likely real demand or channel stuffing. Output a Markdown report saved to disk with source annotations, a data table, and a conclusion paragraph.'):
1. Inspect CSV structure: Read offline_data/regional_sales.csv: list all column names, total row count, date range (min/max month), unique regions, unique product lines, and sample 5 rows → db_agent
2. Compute 24-month rolling mean & volume ratio: For each (region × product_line) pair, compute the 24-month trailing mean of monthly sales volume, then compute the ratio = current_month_volume / 24-month_mean for every month. Save the full result table to a CSV file (e.g. offline_data/volume_ratio_analysis.csv) → code_agent
3. Identify top-3 volume spikes & fetch return rates: From the ratio CSV, find the top-3 (region, product_line, month) combinations by highest ratio. For each, also extract the return_rate for that same month from the original CSV. Save a small summary table → code_agent
4. Assess demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 spikes, compute supporting signals: (a) return rate at spike month vs 24-month avg return rate, (b) whether the following 1-2 months show a volume drop (reversal), (c) whether the spike is isolated or part of a trend. Save a structured assessment table → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report: Write a complete Markdown report to disk (e.g. offline_data/volume_spike_report.md) containing: H1 title, a data table of top-3 spikes with ratio & return rate, source annotations on every key number in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）', and a concluding paragraph judging real demand vs channel stuffing. All data from local CSV only. → code_agent
